title image: space_paint, whole copies with even ground gaps
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, deep-read one council-rota doc, Rye-first, send each increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think The compositing family stood at three verbs: compose (paint_over, src-over blit), compose_tiled (paint_tiled, CSS background-repeat: repeat -- tiles and CLIPS the boundary copy), place_paint (paint_placed, CSS background-position + no-repeat -- one anchored copy). The CSS background-repeat property has exactly three visual modes; the tree held repeat and no-repeat but not the third, `space`. That gap made space_paint the clear Lindy-first crux-first next rung: it COMPLETES a named CSS family (a durable, closed set a reader learns once), it is tractable in the family's own discipline (route to compose, no new pixel loop), and it exercises real gap-distribution arithmetic rather than restating a sibling.
think Design: paint_spaced(target, x, y, w, h, pattern). The CSS `space` rule: fit only WHOLE copies (never clip to make one fit), pin the first and last flush to the two edges, distribute the leftover as even gaps between them. Per axis, count = floor(box/unit) whole copies; copy i seats at i*unit + (i*total_gap)/(count-1) with integer division, so copy 0 lands at 0 and copy count-1 at (count-1)*unit + total_gap = box - unit (flush), monotonic and disjoint (consecutive offsets differ by at least unit). The distinctive property vs compose_tiled: the gaps stay GROUND -- the pattern shows between the copies, never through them.
think Two honest edges the axis plan folds in without a special path in the loop. When only one whole copy fits (count 1), axis_offset returns 0 -- the lone copy seats at the start, the leftover trailing as ground (CSS `space` with one image). When the pattern is LARGER than the box (floor gives 0), plan_axis falls back to count 1 with span = box, so a single copy is CLIPPED to the box's top-left window -- the family's oversize rule (compose_tiled and place_paint both clip an oversize source), kept here so the three verbs agree at the boundary. The two axes are planned independently, so a box can space on one axis and clip on the other.
think Compose not braid held exactly as the siblings: compose.paint_over_region OWNS the blit, qoi owns both buffers; space_paint only ROUTES each whole copy to its spaced offset -- no new blend math, no new codec, no new color, not even a new pixel loop. All arithmetic is u32 and proven wrap-free (box <= qoi_max_dim 8192, i*total_gap <= box, i*unit < box), the box bound-checked once up front in u64, all-or-nothing so a refusal paints nothing.
think Rota this lap deep-read item 25, active-designing/20260816-205859_double-seat-expansion-eight-seasons.md (the eight-season map). It names Season G Open Media Primitives as the open, bounded, permissively-licensed media family -- image (QOI/HUNK) and audio (ALES) standing, the color/font/video and terminal rungs finishing it. space_paint sits squarely in that season: a bounded, asserted, explicit-width compositing primitive that prepares Brushstroke and Skate with a proven background model the day the design system wakes, and waits on nothing paused (only Brushstroke rendering is held, not the geometry beneath it).
obs GREEN on the first build and first witness run -- no red this lap. The apostrophe-in-witness lantern (REDS #76 -> #85) is already closed for this family's template via `assert selftest.out contains`, which the new witness inherits; the printed GREEN line carries no apostrophe regardless, so the guard is safe twice over.
obs The whole CSS background-repeat family now reads as one closed set in Rye: repeat (compose_tiled, clips), no-repeat (place_paint, one anchored), space (space_paint, whole copies with ground gaps). The one CSS mode still unbuilt is `round`, which SCALES tiles to a whole count -- that needs a resampler (a real new pixel loop), so it rightly waits for the scale primitive rather than joining this route-only family.
loom witness=space_paint_witness build=green selftest=green tame_style=clean width_check=exit0 ascii=clean
file image/space_paint.rye the CSS background-repeat: space verb (paint_spaced, plan_axis, axis_offset), GREEN
file tools/space_paint_witness.rish proves it on metal -- an exact fill with no ground, a leftover axis showing the gap as ground with first/last flush, one whole copy at the start, an oversize pattern clipped to one copy, a translucent src-over fill, a QOI round trip, a sub-rectangle, refusals by name
file image/README.md names space_paint.rye beside place_paint.rye, completing the background-repeat family (docs-sync)
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge + Git nib refreshed to the space_paint rung (nib PENDING until the work commit, amended once per remember-git-nib rule)
recommend keep-going the open-media family continues -- the CSS background-repeat triad is now whole; next agent-doable rungs could be an alpha-mask compose (draw a picture through a stencil), object-fit contain/cover (which needs a nearest-neighbor scaler first, a real new pixel loop and its own rung), or a background-position with an edge inset (a margin variant of place_paint); all agent-doable, no gate reached.
